+**Movement and goods:** **Ship uses a Waterway (blue connection); Wagon uses a Road (brown connection).** Either action moves your Merchant to one adjacent town along just one connection. You may take **one** good from that connection, choosing one if several lie there, and keep it beside your board. Empty Roads/Waterways are legal and yield no good. Movement itself does not build Trading Stations.
 
 **Building:** Guildhall requires your Merchant in the town. A town with any player's Trading Station cannot receive another. **Orléans is the exception: each player may build one station there.** Only built stations count for income and final scoring.
 
